Z||000000||85ZainoGT||08-14-2001||10:47 AM||||Ok, I am going to the 1/4 mile track tonight, what should I expect from my stock 85gt (2.8L)?  1/4? 60'? trap speed?  thanks...<p>[This message has been edited by 85ZainoGT (edited 08-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||banditbalz||08-14-2001||12:22 PM||||You running an auto or a 4 speed? Hopefully it's the 4 gear. You can expect 60' times of 2-2.2 depending on your rpm's at launch. I like to launch around 3250 with 20 psi in the rear tires. 1/4 mile should be around 15.7 -16.0 depending on tranny. Trap speed will be in the neighbourhood of 86 mp/h. Pull redline in first and second gear and hold it through third. If you have a slushbox, you can knock a full second off these times. A few simple mods like a holley scoop and/or cold air intake may knock a tenth or two off your times. It worked for me.<BR>I have achieved a best of 15.2 at 90 mp/h on my stock (only a Holley scoop) 170,000 km motor.<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/HardLaunch_4.jpg">    <BR>currently being updated ---&gt; <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/banditbalz/" TARGET=_blank>www.geocities.com/banditbalz/</A> <P><BR>------------------<BR>Silver 86 GT<BR>completely stock,<BR>completely fast!<P><p>[This message has been edited by banditbalz (edited 08-14-2001).]||||reg||12
